/// Chapter 12 of the guide, written from md-docs/12-styling.md by
/// scripts/site-from-guide.py; edit the guide, not this file.
page Styling(path: "/docs/guide/styling", title: "Styling", description: "Design tokens and themes, style blocks with splices and nesting, transitions, classes, dark mode and layout.", layout: DocsShell("Styling", chapter: "Chapter 12", blurb: "Every built-in ships styled; a theme changes the whole site; a style block is real CSS scoped to its element.", sections: [Anchor(id: "design-tokens-and-the-theme", label: "Design tokens and the theme"), Anchor(id: "style", label: "style \{ \}"), Anchor(id: "transition", label: "transition \{ \}"), Anchor(id: "classes-and-your-own-stylesheet", label: "Classes and your own stylesheet"), Anchor(id: "enum-props-as-hooks", label: "Enum props as hooks"), Anchor(id: "dark-mode", label: "Dark mode"), Anchor(id: "layout-without-css", label: "Layout without CSS"), Anchor(id: "what-the-build-emits", label: "What the build emits")], prevTo: "/docs/guide/expressions", prevLabel: "11. Expressions", nextTo: "/docs/guide/motion", nextLabel: "13. Motion")) {
    Stack(gap: .lg) {
        Markdown("Every built-in ships styled, and a theme changes the whole site by changing its tokens. When you need more, an element takes a `style \{ \}` block of real CSS, scoped to that element, with tokens and live values spliced in.")

        Heading("Design tokens and the theme", id: "design-tokens-and-the-theme").h2

        Markdown("A theme is a set of tokens, each of which becomes a CSS custom property (`--color-primary`). A `theme` declaration overrides what the baseline carries; every token not listed keeps its baseline value:")

        CodeBlock("theme Brand \{\n    color-primary: #0F766E\n    color-secondary: #134E4A\n    color-background: #FFFFFF\n    color-surface: #F8FAFC\n    color-text: #0F172A\n    color-text-muted: #64748B\n    color-border: #E2E8F0\n    font-family: 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif\n    font-family-mono: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace\n    radius-md: 14px\n    spacing-lg: 2.5rem\n    shadow-md: 0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.08)\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("A project with one theme uses it; with several, `webfluent.app.json` chooses: `\"theme\": \{ \"name\": \"Brand\" \}`. Values are raw CSS to the end of the line.\n\nThe baseline tokens, by group:")

        Table(caption: "Design tokens and the theme") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Group").header
                    Table.Cell("Tokens").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Color")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`color-primary`, `color-secondary`, `color-success`, `color-danger`, `color-warning`, `color-info`, `color-background`, `color-surface`, `color-text`, `color-text-muted`, `color-border`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Font")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`font-family`, `font-family-mono`, `font-size-xs` … `font-size-3xl`, `font-weight-normal/medium/bold`, `line-height-tight/normal/loose`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Spacing")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`spacing-xs`, `spacing-sm`, `spacing-md`, `spacing-lg`, `spacing-xl`, `spacing-2xl`, `spacing-3xl`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Radius")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`radius-none`, `radius-sm`, `radius-md`, `radius-lg`, `radius-xl`, `radius-full`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Shadow")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`shadow-none`, `shadow-sm`, `shadow-md`, `shadow-lg`, `shadow-xl`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Motion")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`transition-fast`, `transition-normal`, `transition-slow`") }
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("A theme may add tokens of its own (`surface-raised: #131519`); they become custom properties like the rest. The contrast lint (`A13`) checks text against background pairs in the theme and warns below WCAG AA.\n\n`theme.builtin` in `webfluent.app.json`: `full` (default) ships the baseline look of every built-in you use; `structural` ships only their layout and mechanics — focus rings, overlays, the grid — for a site that brings its whole design.")

        Heading("style \{ \}", id: "style").h2

        CodeBlock("page Styled(path: \"/\") \{\n    state accent = \"#D97706\"\n    state wide = false\n    Card \{\n        style \{\n            padding: $lg                       // a token, resolved by the property: spacing-lg\n            background: $surface               // color-surface\n            border: 1px solid $border\n            border-radius: $radius-lg\n            box-shadow: $shadow-md\n            border-left: 4px solid \{accent\}    // a live value: repaints when `accent` changes\n            max-width: \{if wide \{ \"100%\" \} else \{ \"40rem\" \}\}\n            &:hover \{ box-shadow: $shadow-lg \}\n            & > p \{ margin: 0 \}\n            @media (max-width: 640px) \{ padding: $sm \}\n        \}\n        Text(\"Styled card\")\n        Button(\"Widen\") \{ on click \{ wide = !wide \} \}\n    \}\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("- A style block holds CSS declarations, one per line or `;`-separated. No quotes around values — `padding: 2rem`, not `\"2rem\"`.\n- `$token` names a token. A short name is resolved by the property: `padding: $lg` is `spacing-lg`, `color: $primary` is `color-primary`, `border-radius: $lg` is `radius-lg`, `box-shadow: $md` is `shadow-md`, `font-size: $xl` is `font-size-xl`, `transition: $fast`. A full name (`$color-primary`, `$surface-raised`) works anywhere. A token the theme does not have is an error.\n- `\{expr\}` splices a live value; the declaration updates when the value changes. A whole value or a part of one (`\{n\}px`).\n- `&:hover`, `&:focus-visible`, `&.active`, `& > p`, `&[aria-current]` nest as CSS nesting does; `@media (…) \{ \}` nests too.\n- The block is scoped: it becomes a class on that element alone, written to the page's stylesheet at build time. Splices become custom properties set by the runtime.\n\nThe static parts of every `style \{ \}` are compiled to CSS; the linter warns when a declaration is invalid CSS.")

        Heading("transition \{ \}", id: "transition").h2

        CodeBlock("page Fade(path: \"/\") \{\n    state on = false\n    Card \{\n        style \{ opacity: \{if on \{ 1 \} else \{ 0.4 \}\}; transform: \{if on \{ \"none\" \} else \{ \"scale(0.98)\" \}\} \}\n        transition \{ opacity: $fast; transform: 200ms ease-out \}\n        Text(\"Fades\")\n    \}\n    Button(\"Toggle\") \{ on click \{ on = !on \} \}\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("`transition \{ prop: duration easing \}` sets CSS transitions for the element; a `$fast/$normal/$slow` token or a raw value. Reduced-motion readers get none ([chapter 13](/docs/guide/motion)).")

        Heading("Classes and your own stylesheet", id: "classes-and-your-own-stylesheet").h2

        Markdown("`class: \"name\"` adds a class from your own stylesheet; a `.css` file in `src/` is bundled into `styles.css`, and `meta.stylesheets` in `webfluent.app.json` links external ones.")

        CodeBlock("page Classes(path: \"/\") \{\n    state active = true\n    Container(class: \"hero\") \{\n        Heading(\"Welcome\", class: if active \{ \"title is-on\" \} else \{ \"title\" \}).h1\n    \}\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("The value may be an expression, so a class can follow state. Built-ins wear `wf-*` classes (`wf-btn`, `wf-btn--primary`, `wf-card`), stable across releases, so a stylesheet may target them.")

        Heading("Enum props as hooks", id: "enum-props-as-hooks").h2

        Markdown("A component's enum props are written to its root element as `data-<prop>`, so one stylesheet rule styles every variant ([chapter 8](/docs/guide/components#enum-props)):")

        CodeBlock(".note[data-tone=\"loud\"] \{ font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-danger) \}", title: "css")

        Heading("Dark mode", id: "dark-mode").h2

        Markdown("A second `theme` declaration named in `webfluent.app.json` as `\"theme\": \{ \"name\": \"Light\", \"dark\": \"Night\" \}` stands in for dark mode. Its tokens override the light theme's under the reader's system preference (`prefers-color-scheme: dark`) and whenever `setTheme(\"dark\")` was called; `setTheme(\"light\")` forces light, `setTheme(\"system\")` follows the system again. The choice is remembered across visits and applied before the first paint, so a dark reader never sees a light flash.")

        CodeBlock("theme Light \{\n    color-background: #FFFFFF\n    color-text: #0F172A\n\}\n\ntheme Night \{\n    color-background: #0B1220\n    color-surface: #111827\n    color-text: #E5E7EB\n    color-text-muted: #9CA3AF\n    color-border: #1F2937\n\}\n\npage Prefs(path: \"/\") \{\n    Text(\"You are on the \{theme\} theme\")\n    Row(gap: .sm) \{\n        Button(\"Light\") \{ on click \{ setTheme(\"light\") \} \}\n        Button(\"Dark\") \{ on click \{ setTheme(\"dark\") \} \}\n        Button(\"System\") \{ on click \{ setTheme(\"system\") \} \}\n    \}\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("Everything that uses tokens — the built-ins, your `$token` styles — switches with it; a color written raw does not, so prefer tokens. The `theme` value is `\"light\"`, `\"dark\"` or `\"system\"`.")

        Heading("Layout without CSS", id: "layout-without-css").h2

        Markdown("Most layout needs no `style` at all: `Stack`, `Row`, `Grid`, `Container`, `Spacer` and `Divider` with their `gap:`, `align:`, `justify:`, `columns:` props ([chapter 4](/docs/guide/elements#layout)), plus the responsive `viewport` values ([chapter 5](/docs/guide/state#the-browser-as-values)).")

        CodeBlock("page Layout(path: \"/\") \{\n    Container \{\n        Stack(gap: .lg) \{\n            Row(justify: .between, align: .center) \{\n                Heading(\"Projects\").h2\n                Button(\"New\").primary.sm\n            \}\n            Grid(columns: if viewport.md \{ 3 \} else \{ 1 \}, gap: .md) \{\n                for n in 1..=6 \{ Card \{ Text(\"Project \{n\}\") \} \}\n            \}\n        \}\n    \}\n\}", title: "wf")

        Heading("What the build emits", id: "what-the-build-emits").h2

        Markdown("`styles.css` holds the tokens (`:root \{ --color-primary: … \}`), the dark overrides, the structural and baseline CSS of the built-ins you used (and only those), and your bundled stylesheets. Each page's own `style` blocks go to `pages/<Name>.css`, loaded with the page. Unused built-in CSS is pruned.")
    }
}
